     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Graph the system, then identify which graph matches what you drew.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x - 3y \\le 5\"></span>Graph the first line as a solid line using the intercepts <span data-math=\"\\left( {\\frac{5}{2},0} \\right)\"></span>and <span data-math=\"\\left( {0, - \\frac{5}{3}} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Test (0, 0).</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2\\left( 0 \\right) + 3\\left( 0 \\right) \\le 5\"></span></p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"0 \\le 5\"></span></td>\n<td>This is true. Shade lightly the side where (0, 0) is located.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Second line: <span data-math=\"x - y \\ge 3\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Graph the second line as a solid line using the intercepts <span data-math=\"\\left( {3,0} \\right)\"></span>and <span data-math=\"\\left( {0, - 3} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Test (0, 0).</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"0 - 0 \\ge 3\"></span></td>\n<td>This is false. Shade lightly the side where (0, 0) is not located.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The solution is the region shaded by both graphs.</p>"
    }
   ],
